If you want a good example of what to make it look like, simply look at any 
good turn-based RPG.  Lets take Final Fantasy Tactics for example, or even 
Final Fantasy Tactics Advance.  While the game is waiting for your input 
the characters have a sort of waiting animation.  The characters sort of 
march in place, the monsters sway back and forth, etc.  It seems like a 
small thing but this really helps to make the game come alive.  Just 
because it's turn-based does not mean the only time you see movement on the 
screen is when you do something!


